## Context

The 2026-07 home reorg had to be applied twice to the same fact: once in
`scripts/projects.json` (PR #493) and once in `scripts/setup-claude-agent.sh`'s
hardcoded `PROJECTS` array (PR #497, ticket 0284). The /gaze simplify pass on
PR #497 flagged the duplication and correctly scoped the refactor out of that
string-sweep diff. `scripts/projects.json` is the canonical registry; the
setup script should derive its list from it (jq is available) so the next
path change lands in one place.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/setup-claude-agent.sh` — hardcoded PROJECTS array
- `scripts/projects.json` — canonical registry

## Actions

1. Replace the PROJECTS array with a jq read of projects.json (tilde
   expansion handled as projects.json consumers do).
2. Check other scripts for hardcoded copies of the same list.

## Exit criteria

- setup-claude-agent.sh has no hardcoded project list; behavior unchanged
  for existing projects; a registry edit propagates without touching the
  script.
